  "label": "The man in the image is mapped as the embodiment of the hateful stereotype being described.",
  "description": "The visual of the stern-faced man with crossed arms is used to represent the hateful stereotype that Black people are hypersensitive to the smell of 'nigger'. The man's confrontational posture and expression visually reinforce the accusatory and hostile tone of the text, creating an analogical mapping where the man symbolizes the stereotype being presented. The text 'they can't stand the smell of ni**er either!' is mapped onto the man's visual presence, implying he is the personification of the stereotype's accusation.",
